    <string name="nutri_score_info_desc">Nutri-Score evaluates 100g of food by balancing negative points (energy, sugars, saturated fat, sodium) against positive points (fiber, protein, fruit, vegetable &amp; nut content).</string>
    <string name="nutri_score_info_grades">• Grade A (Green): Highest nutritional balance\n• Grade B (Light Green): Good nutritional balance\n• Grade C (Yellow): Balanced nutrition\n• Grade D (Orange): High in sugar, fat, or salt\n• Grade E (Red): Poor nutritional quality; consume in moderation</string>
    <string name="nova_info_desc">The NOVA classification categorizes food by the extent and purpose of industrial food processing (developed by the University of São Paulo, Brazil):</string>
    <string name="nova_info_grades">• NOVA 1: Unprocessed or minimally processed foods (whole plants, seeds, eggs, meat, milk)\n• NOVA 2: Processed culinary ingredients (oils, butter, sugar, salt)\n• NOVA 3: Processed foods (canned vegetables, cheese, cured meats, artisan breads)\n• NOVA 4: Ultra-processed food products (industrial formulations with colorings, flavor enhancers, high-fructose syrups, and emulsifiers)</string>
    <string name="eco_score_info_desc">Eco-Score measures the environmental footprint of food products using Agribalyse life cycle analysis (carbon, water, land use, ecotoxicity) plus bonuses and penalties for packaging recyclability and organic farming labels.</string>
    <string name="eco_score_info_grades">• Grade A: Very low environmental impact\n• Grade B: Low environmental impact\n• Grade C: Moderate impact\n• Grade D: High impact\n• Grade E: Very high environmental impact</string>

